---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ArticleCTA from '../../components/ArticleCTA.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/playlists-not-showing-cdj#article',
  headline: 'Playlists Not Showing on CDJ - Causes and Fixes',
  description: 'Your USB mounts, tracks play, but playlists are missing on the CDJ. The database didn\'t make it. Here\'s the 5-minute fix and the permanent one.',
  author: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.savemygig.com/#org' },
  datePublished: '2026-07-24',
  dateModified: '2026-07-27',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://www.savemygig.com/fix/playlists-not-showing-cdj',
};
---
<Base
  title="Playlists Not Showing on CDJ or XDJ? Here's Why | Save My Gig!"
  description="Your USB mounts, tracks play, but playlists are missing on the CDJ. The database didn't make it. Here's the 5-minute fix and the permanent one."
  path="/fix/playlists-not-showing-cdj"
  ogImage="/og/playlists-not-showing-cdj.png"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <main class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <div class="status-line red">Playlists_Missing</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">PLAYLISTS NOT SHOWING<br>ON THE <span class="danger">CDJ</span>?</h1>

    <div class="panel panel-danger">
      <p style="margin:0"><strong>Short version:</strong> if tracks play but playlists are missing, your music arrived, the Rekordbox database didn't. Either the export skipped it, the eject corrupted it, or the drive was filled by drag-and-drop instead of Rekordbox.</p>
    </div>

        <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">Why it happens</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><strong>Files were dragged onto the USB in Finder/Explorer</strong>, that copies music, not the database. Playlists only exist after a Rekordbox EXPORT-mode sync.</li>
      <li><strong>The export was interrupted or ejected unsafely</strong>, the database is written near the end of a sync; pull early and tracks survive but playlists don't.</li>
      <li><strong>Mixed exports from two computers</strong>, a second computer's Rekordbox can overwrite the device database with its own (empty) view.</li>
      <li><strong>Very old player firmware</strong> meeting a new Rekordbox database version.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">At the venue (5 minutes)</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>No laptop? Use <span class="mono">SOURCE → USB → FOLDER</span>, your music is still playable by folder, tonight is safe.</li>
      <li>With a laptop: open Rekordbox in <span class="mono">EXPORT</span> mode, connect the USB, drag tonight's playlists onto the device, wait for the full sync, eject with the Rekordbox button.</li>
      <li>Re-insert on the player and check the <span class="mono">PLAYLIST</span> browse tab, not FOLDER.</li>
    </ul>

    
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="acc-sec" name="fix-acc">
      <summary><h2 class="acc-h2">The permanent fix</h2><span class="acc-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="acc-body">
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>One rule: <strong>music gets on gig drives only via Rekordbox export.</strong> Never Finder, never Explorer.</li>
      <li>One computer owns the drive. If you must use two, let one be the only writer.</li>
      <li>After every library change: re-export, eject properly, verify the playlists load before leaving home.</li>
    </ul>
      </div>
    </details>



    <ArticleCTA article="playlists_missing" />
  </main>
</Base>
